The point of the game is to win, i.e., ascend. We can debate endlessly
about how the scoring is broken, Gehennom is boring, yada yada, but
the goal of the game of Nethack remains: offer the amulet to your god/
dess at the high altar, and attain demigod/dess status. Therefore, a
strategy such as the protection racket to lower your AC as quickly and
cheaply as possible, would naturally have as its goal making ascension
easier, or more assured. Unless I hear that a sizable number of
players who are actually winning the game are using the protection
racket as a primary tool for doing so, I can't believe that it's that
useful of a strategy.

